11-10 16:43:36     [harness 42.1s, 16 turns, opus $0.4046 176977+3915 tok] {"summary": "I placed one restock order for 22 food units and left all prices as they were.\n\n**Where the shop stands:** Book is 421.6M and the overall score is 0.736. Stars are 4.42 and we made 120 sales in the last 6 hours. Our 220 units in stock cost 100.4M, and 63 of them have been on the shelf more than a day.\n\n**What I bought:** Only fast-selling food that was running low, using each category's best-selling SKUs:\n- **Processed meat:** 5 Buffalo wings and 3 Buffalo drumsticks. We sold 29 in the last 6 hours and had only 5 left.\n- **Kimchi:** 4 chonggak kimchi, 2 green-onion kimchi and 2 cabbage kimchi. Kimchi is the market's biggest category, and many of our current units are close to expiry.\n- **Dessert:** 2 macaron boxes. We sold 12 in 6 hours and had none left.\n- **Fresh fruit:** 2 boxes of apples and 2 of dried jujubes. Fruit is 9% of market sales and we had 2 units.\n\nMy first order asked for 3 each of the dessert and fruit items. The server allows at most 2 units of food that keeps 48 hours, so I resubmitted them at 2.\n\n**What I didn't buy:** No furniture. Our 22 sofas cost about 2.7–2.8M each, against a market median of 2.61M. Our 16 stone beds cost about 1.72M each against 1.51M, and they've all been in stock 37–95 hours. Buying more would only add stock we can't sell at a profit. One more sofa was bought about an hour ago under an earlier plan; this new plan replaces that one.\n\n**Why prices are unchanged:**\n- The seller's price tests don't show lower opening prices closing more deals in any category. For sofas and beds the lowest price tested closed the fewest deals (5% and 9%), and the highest closed the most.\n- Cutting sofa and bed prices toward the market level would mean selling below what we paid, which the seller won't do and which would reduce Book. We'll keep holding them at cost, since unsold stock still counts at cost in Book.\n- In the categories that sell well (processed meat, kimchi, water and drinks, snacks), the current prices already close deals at a healthy rate.\n\n**Problems to watch:**\n- Buyers refused to pay for some of our items because they lacked a required certificate, had no warranty, or had too little shelf life left. I chose items that keep up to 30 days for this order, except the dessert and fruit.\n- The sofa SKU has three low reviews saying it broke.\n- One buyer posted that our soy milk had 51.5 hours of shelf life left when they needed 72.", "categories_boosted": ["식품>육류>가공/조리 육류", "식품>김치/반찬/즉석요리>김치", "식품>기타 가공식품>디저트", "식품>야채/과일>신선과일(부패주의)"], "categories_dropped": ["가구/침구>가구>소파/의자/스툴", "가구/침구>가구>침대/매트리스"]}
